course: dictionary
lesson: 8810
title: Words for people and their work
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A shearer is a person whose job is to cut the wool off sheep. The ending -er is a clue: it often names someone who does a job, like a baker who bakes. A shearer can also be a machine that shears, or cuts, so the context tells you which one is meant.
explain: «Farm sheep grow wool that never stops growing, so every spring a shearer gives them a haircut.» The clues are sheep, wool and haircut, so a shearer here cuts the wool. Try the swap: "every spring a person who cuts the wool gives them a haircut" still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Some words describe how well someone does a job. «A good shearer» means someone who is skilled at the work. «A good shearer taking about two minutes per sheep» tells you that a skilled shearer is quick, because two minutes is a short time for one sheep.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A shearer is a person, or a machine, that cuts the wool off sheep.
fact: Shearing is hard physical work, and shearers often travel from farm to farm in shearing season.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, shearers usually work in a woolshed.
fact: A fast shearer can shear hundreds of sheep in one day.
fact: «Gun shearer» is Australian and New Zealand slang for a very fast, skilled shearer.
exercise: What is a shearer's job? | To keep sheep warm in winter | To sell wool in a shop | *To cut the wool off sheep | To drive sheep to market
exercise: «Gun shearer» is slang for what? | A gun that shoots sheep | A farmer who owns many sheep | A machine that washes wool | *A very fast, skilled shearer
exercise: «A good shearer taking about two minutes per sheep» tells you what about a skilled shearer? | They are asleep most of the day | They never touch the wool | *They work quickly | They are very big and strong
test: Which word names a person or machine that shears? | haircut | woolshed | *shearer | sheep
test: «A fast shearer can shear hundreds of sheep in one day.» What does this tell you? | *They are quick and skilled at the job | They only shear goats | They work very slowly | They never leave the farm
exam: Where do shearers usually work in Australia and New Zealand? | A school | A castle | *A woolshed | A supermarket
